cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ProvenanceEventTree: event tree analysis with an evidence ledger"
message: "Please cite the method as well as this tool."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23139763
authors:
  - family-names: Inderwildi
    given-names: Oliver
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4315-7839"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/oliverinderwildi/systems-analysis/tree/main/src/provenance-event-tree"
abstract: >-
  An implementation of event tree analysis in which the initiating frequency and every barrier
  probability must arrive with a provenance record, each accident sequence inherits the weakest
  evidence class among the barriers that failed on it, and the authorship of every element -
  source, analyst or language model - is recorded and reported.
keywords:
  - event tree analysis
  - reliability
  - risk analysis
  - evidence ledger
  - provenance
  - systems analysis
